PART ONE — OPEN SOURCE, APACHE LICENCE 2.0

The six packages published to npm under the `@xplainer/` scope are licensed
under the Apache Licence, Version 2.0:

    apps/cli                 @xplainer/cli
    packages/mcp-server      @xplainer/mcp-server
    packages/protocol        @xplainer/protocol
    packages/render-core     @xplainer/render-core
    packages/skill           @xplainer/skill
    packages/tts-client      @xplainer/tts-client

Everything inside those six directories is Apache-2.0, including the Remotion
workspace template and the scaffold templates under `packages/render-core`.
The full licence text is in LICENSE-APACHE-2.0 at the root of this repository,
and a copy of it is committed as `LICENSE` inside each of the six package
directories so that it also travels inside every published tarball. The
attribution notice Apache-2.0 section 4(d) propagates is the NOTICE file, at
the root and inside each of the six.

Each of those six manifests declares `"license": "Apache-2.0"`. That SPDX
identifier is the authoritative statement for machine consumers.

    Licensed under the Apache Licence, Version 2.0 (the "Licence"); you may
    not use these files except in compliance with the Licence. You may obtain
    a copy of the Licence at

        http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

    Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software
    distributed under the Licence is distributed on an "AS IS" BASIS, WITHOUT
    WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied. See the
    Licence for the specific language governing permissions and limitations
    under the Licence.


PART TWO — PROPRIETARY, ALL RIGHTS RESERVED

Every other file in this repository is proprietary. No permission is granted
to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, or sell any part
of it. This covers, without being limited to:

    apps/desktop             the desktop client                (tier: open-later)
    packages/config          shared build presets and tooling  (tier: open-later)
    services/tts-sidecar     the packaged TTS sidecar          (tier: open-later)

    infra/, scripts/, docs/, and every other file at the root

No `hosted` member remains in this repository. `apps/api`, `apps/web` and
`services/media-service` were relocated to a private repository on 2026-09-06
(ADR 0023) and this file stopped listing them when they went; that tier stays
proprietary wherever it lives.

The three `open-later` members listed above are on a path to being opened but
have NOT been relicensed: opening the six published packages did not open them,
and each still declares `"license": "UNLICENSED"` in its own manifest. Nothing
in Part One extends to them. Making this repository public did not change that
either — it made them readable, not usable.

The tier each package belongs to is declared in its own package.json as
`"xplainer": { "tier": "hosted" | "open-later" }`, and the boundary between
the tiers is machine-checked. The tier field describes intent; this file
describes the grant. Where they appear to disagree, this file and the
`license` field of the package's own manifest govern.


THIRD PARTY COMPONENTS

Rendering depends on Remotion, which is licensed commercially by Remotion AG
on its own terms. The Apache-2.0 grant in Part One covers this software only;
it grants you nothing in respect of Remotion, and depending on the size of
your company and how you use it you may need your own Remotion licence. See
https://remotion.pro/license and the NOTICE file.


